# ==============================================================================
# GemmaAudit: Fully Offline & Air-Gapped Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# This file contains configuration keys to run the entire analysis engine offline,
# prioritising local inference of Gemma 4 parameter sets tuned via Unsloth.
#
# Copy this file to '.env' to enable your custom configurations:
# cp .env.example .env
#
# ==============================================================================

# --- LLM Backend Configuration ---
# Options:
#   - local_llm: Run real-time local model inference via Ollama/llama.cpp/LM Studio (highly recommended)
#   - emulated:  Run high-fidelity deterministic agent emulator grounded in static analysis
#   - gemini:    (Fallback) Use online Gemini Pro API if internet access is available
LLM_BACKEND=local_llm

# --- Local Offline LLM API Endpoint ---
# Point this to your local model server.
# For Ollama:         http://localhost:11434/v1
# For llama.cpp:      http://localhost:8080/v1
# For LM Studio:      http://localhost:1234/v1
# For vLLM:           http://localhost:8000/v1
LOCAL_LLM_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# --- Local Model Identifier ---
# The identifier of the local offline model to query.
# If you fine-tuned Gemma 4 with Unsloth and exported it to GGUF,
# enter the local Ollama/llama.cpp model name here.
#
# GemmaAudit speaks the standard OpenAI /chat/completions protocol, so ANY
# model your local server exposes works as a drop-in. The agent loop and the
# JCL/COBOL enrichment passes were validated end-to-end against the models
# below — pick whatever is already pulled on your machine to clone-and-run:
#
# Examples:
#   - gemma4-unsloth (custom local GGUF model — the intended target)
#   - qwen3:8b       (verified: 15 KG paragraph nodes enriched cleanly)
#   - llama3:8b      (verified: works as a stock-Ollama fallback)
#   - gemma2         (standard local Gemma 2 / 9B model)
#   - gemma:2b       (fast, lightweight 2B model for low-VRAM machines)
#
# Note: reasoning-mode models (qwen3, deepseek-r1, qwq) emit <think>...</think>
# blocks — backend/llm_client.py strips these automatically, so enrichment
# output stays clean regardless of which model you choose.
LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=gemma4-unsloth

# --- Online Fallback API Key (Optional) ---
# Only needed if LLM_BACKEND=gemini or if local LLM fails and you wish to use online API.
# Leave blank for absolute offline, air-gapped security!
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ==============================================================================
#  UNSLOTH TO OLLAMA EXPORT CHEATSHEET
# ==============================================================================
#
# If you have fine-tuned Gemma 4 using Unsloth, you can export it to a local 4-bit 
# QLoRA GGUF and run it completely offline in Ollama using these steps:
#
# 1. In your Unsloth notebook, save the model as GGUF:
#    model.save_pretrained_gguf("gemma4-unsloth", tokenizer, quantization_method="q4_k_m")
#
# 2. Create a 'Modelfile' next to the exported gguf file with these contents:
#    FROM ./gemma4-unsloth-Q4_K_M.gguf
#    PARAMETER temperature 0.3
#    SYSTEM "You are GemmaAudit, an advanced local modernization consultant..."
#
# 3. Create and register the model inside your local Ollama instance:
#    ollama create gemma4-unsloth -f ./Modelfile
#
# 4. Spin up Ollama and set 'LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=gemma4-unsloth' above!
# ==============================================================================
